  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nUpper ridging over the western U.S. will remain the dominant \nforce this weekend with triple digit heat during the afternoon \nhours today. Low temperatures this morning will struggle to get \ndown to the upper 60s to lower 70s, making for uncomfortable \nsleeping conditions for those without air conditioning. The \nExtreme Heat Warning continues through 10pm this evening. \n\nNighttime Microphysics on GOES Satellite showcase a large red \nsmoke plume stretched from eastern Oregon to north central Montana\nwhich is pretty high in the atmosphere. Air Quality sensors \nacross western Montana at higher elevations are quickly trending \nair quality down across those areas and HRRR/RAP Smoke models are \nindicating that this will get caught in the boundary layer this \nafternoon and dragged down into the Little Rockies and Missouri \nBreaks. Mixing and mid level intensities of smoke concentrations \ncan be hit-and-miss when coming out of the mountains. Therefore \nthe intensity of the visibility drop and areal extent as it \nreaches the surface are low confidence. However, we should not be \nsurprised is a dense Smoke Advisory and air quality alert were to\ngo out by mid-afternoon and this will need to be monitored. \n\nEnsembles continue to show the hot temperatures continuing through\nat least mid-week and possibly into the weekend with highs in the\n90s to around 100 degrees each day. Heat Advisories each \nafternoon after today across varying areas may be necessary as we \nget closer. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNBM Deviations include... slightly lower MinRH today and tomorrow\nafternoon to mesh up with neighbors, Higher hourly PoPs through \n6AM for exiting morning showers, and HRRR/RAP blends to enhance \nvisibility reductions due to smoke through the day. \n\nThere is MODERATE to HIGH confidence in the heat products through\ntoday.\n\nThere is LOW confidence for a dying thunderstorms to produce a \nburst of wind across Petroleum and Garfield county this evening. \n\nThere is MODERATE to HIGH confidence in haze reducing visibility \nas low as 4 SM this evening. \n\nThere is LOW to MODERATE confidence in a visibility drops from\nsmoke becoming low enough for a Dense Smoke Advisory across the\nLittle Rockies and Missouri Breaks. \n\nGAH",
